// GDTF authored area-damage FIELD type — "toxic waste pool".
// This is AUTHORED CONTENT (a field-type catalog entry), not balance tuning. It
// loads as a loose `.ron` through the RonAsset<FieldDef> loader (folder-loaded +
// hot-reloadable), keyed by its filename stem `toxic_waste_pool` — the FieldKey a situation's
// authored `fields:` placement (and the on-death spawn effect) references.
//
// A persistent per-tile damage zone: any ganger standing on a fielded cell loses `damage` HP
// per turn (a FLAT drain — no armor matchup, no injury roll, no RNG), UNLESS ANY worn armor
// piece's ArmorType is in `immune_armor_types` (whole-source immunity — the sealed suit
// protects you). This is the "toxic waste pool as initial terrain" example.
//
// CATALOG PROPOSAL (REVIEW-FLAG — the field-type <-> immune-armor pairing is a design
// vocabulary choice; these are defensible interim defaults, surfaced for user review):
//   - damage_type Chem (wheel node 2 — toxin / acid / gas).
//   - immune { Flak, Hazard } — Flak is the Chem-mirror armor node (a sealed toxin vest),
//     Hazard is the hazmat suit; both plausibly seal you against a chemical pool.
//   - Permanent — a fixed terrain hazard that never dissipates.
// The magnitudes are ARBITRARY interim values; tune later (never pinned by a test).
(
    damage:             3,                 // FieldDamage — flat HP drained per turn (bypasses armor)
    damage_type:        Chem,              // wheel-node flavour (presentation only — the tick bypasses the matchup)
    immune_armor_types: [Flak, Hazard],    // whole-source immunity: ANY worn piece of these skips ALL damage
    duration:           Permanent,         // never expires (fixed terrain hazard)
)
